sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Admission and recovery when the broker is unavailable
  accDescr: The API accepts committed work while RabbitMQ is down. The relay retries unsent dispatch. Publication may repeat after an uncertain confirmation, so workers use database claims and unique result writes.
  participant U as React
  participant A as Django
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  participant R as Relay
  participant Q as RabbitMQ
  participant W as Worker
  U->>A: POST job + idempotency key
  A->>D: Atomic Job + Outbox
  D-->>A: Commit
  A-->>U: 202 queued + IDs
  R->>D: Read unsent dispatch
  R--xQ: Publish fails: broker down
  Note over D,R: Intent stays unsent<br/>Job remains queued
  R->>Q: Retry after broker returns
  Q-->>R: Publisher confirm
  R->>D: Mark dispatch sent
  Q->>W: UUID delivery can repeat
  W->>D: Short locked claim + lease token
  Note over W: Extract + validate<br/>Outside transaction
  W->>D: Current token? Score + one result + terminal state
  W-->>Q: Acknowledge completion
  U->>A: GET job status
  A->>D: Owner-scoped read
  A-->>U: succeeded + evidence report
